//! The `marker-start` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property points to a
//! marker that will be drawn on the first vertex of the element's path; that is, at its starting
//! vertex. The marker must have been defined using an SVG `marker` element, and can only be
//! referenced with a `<url>` value. The value of the CSS property overrides any values of the
//! `marker-start` attribute in the SVG.
//!
//! Initial: none. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - none: This means no marker will be drawn at the first vertex of the element's path.
//!
//! Grammar: none | <marker-ref>
//!
//! Specification: https://w3c.github.io/svgwg/svg2-draft/painting.html#MarkerStartProperty
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/marker-start
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

